# The pointer moves when a finger lifts.
#
# This panel reports fuzz 0 on each axis. libinput sizes its hysteresis from
# the kernel fuzz, thus a fuzz of 0 gives no hysteresis and each small movement
# reaches the pointer, including the movement the panel reports as a finger
# lifts and the contact centre shifts.
#
# Measured with evtest, 16 press-and-lift cycles: the lift moves the position
# 1 to 12 units. The axes are 3599 units over 128 mm and 1799 over 81 mm, thus
# 28 and 22 units per mm.
#
# Tuning history, by feel, on this panel:
#   12  drift still visible
#   18  drift gone; slow precise movement feels sticky
#    9  still too much dead zone to place a cursor comfortably
#    3  current. About 0.11 mm on X, 0.14 mm on Y — below the measured drift,
#       thus the lift tail is handled by the pressure range in
#       local-overrides.quirks, not here.
#
# CAUTION: Do not "fix" the remaining drift by raising this again. It was tried
# at 18 and rejected by feel. If the drift needs more work, take it from the
# pressure range in local-overrides.quirks, which ends the contact earlier
# without adding a dead zone to ordinary movement.
#
# Format is EVDEV_ABS_<hex code>=<min>:<max>:<resolution>:<fuzz>. The empty
# fields keep the kernel values. 00 and 01 are ABS_X and ABS_Y; 35 and 36 are
# ABS_MT_POSITION_X and ABS_MT_POSITION_Y.
#
# NOTE: This is the fuzz path, not libinput's quirks path. libinput reads the
# quirks files once when the compositor makes its context, thus a quirks change
# needs a new session. It reads LIBINPUT_FUZZ_* per device, thus this applies
# with `udevadm trigger`.
evdev:name:GXTP5420:00 27C6:0F95 Touchpad:dmi:*svnLENOVO*pvrThinkPadX1CarbonGen14*
 EVDEV_ABS_00=:::3
 EVDEV_ABS_01=:::3
 EVDEV_ABS_35=:::3
 EVDEV_ABS_36=:::3
